FILE: app/src/fly-controls.ts
```ts
import type { FreeCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { attachConfigurableFreeControl } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function attachFlyControls(
  camera: FreeCamera,
  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
  scene: SceneContext,
): () => void {
  return attachConfigurableFreeControl(camera, canvas, scene, {
    upKeys: ["Space"],
    downKeys: ["PageDown"],
    fastKeys: ["ShiftLeft", "ShiftRight"],
    fastMultiplier: 3,
  });
}
```

I added `src/fly-controls.ts` using the library’s configurable free-camera controls, mapping `Space` to rise, `PageDown` to sink, and left/right `Shift` to a 3× speed key while excluding `Shift` from the up/down key lists. I was unsure only about whether `attachConfigurableFreeControl` is exported from the package root versus a deeper module path, and whether its key mappings use `KeyboardEvent.code` names (I assumed they do).
